Light show for the ESP-NOW mesh (needs espnow-mesh.patch)

Adds lib/mesh_sync.py, a clock the badges share over ESP-NOW, and
apps/lights.py, a "Light show" app whose LEDs animate in step on every badge
running it (patterns: rainbow, pulse, chase, flash, cylon; UserA and UserB
change the pattern for the whole group). The badge picks up any app in apps/ by
itself and the app starts the clock, so no existing file changes. Paths are
relative to the badge's root folder, the one holding main.py.

Made against Hack-a-Day/2026-Billboard_Badge at 5945518 (2026-11-08), where
the badge's root folder is firmware/badge. It only adds files, so it applies
to any version of the firmware.

Apply from the folder holding main.py:
    git apply light-show.patch
    (or: patch -p1 < light-show.patch)
Apply from a clone of github.com/Hack-a-Day/2026-Billboard_Badge:
    git apply --directory=firmware/badge light-show.patch
Apply from the supercon10 project root:
    git apply --directory=device patches/light-show.patch
Then copy lib/mesh_sync.py and apps/lights.py to the badge, together with the
lib/espnow_mesh.py from espnow-mesh.patch: the light show needs its newest
version.

Files:
    apps/lights.py       new file, 164 lines
    lib/mesh_sync.py     new file, 172 lines

